<http://hgnc.project-genesis.io#FAMILY_1804> rdfs:label "MicroRNA MIR320 family" ;
    rdfs:comment "In molecular biology mir-320 microRNA is a short RNA molecule. MicroRNAs function to regulate the expression levels of other genes by several mechanisms. The biogenesis of miR-320 is different from the canonical Microprocessor-dependent miRNAs. The pre-miR-320 is transcribed directly as a precursor microRNA hairpin and thus contains a 5' m7G-cap.   " ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://hgnc.project-genesis.io#FAMILY_476> .

